          "certainty": "likely",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/xn585zh2707#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded medium on the figures of the date: one figure is arguable. Pencil, four small figures run together, read from the lower (180-degree) panel. A 6 as a large right-opening curve closing into a bottom bowl, then a 7 with its crossbar, then two 2s, each a closed top loop over a stroke that runs down to a long horizontal base. The two 2s are written slightly differently, one loop rounder than the other, and at this resolution the first of them could be taken for a 3, which would make the year 32; the base stroke is what decides it for 2, so 6.7.22."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       },
       "medium": "pencil"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "scan": "https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/xn585zh2707%2Fxn585zh2707_0001/",
